share":0.17270601857142176,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1875072244402105,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.16058097490005502,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.06610417069367758,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.011200898567907397,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":81.3,"_gate_insider_own":0.1184,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":78.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SiriusPoint Ltd. provides multi-line reinsurance and insurance products and services worldwide. It operates through four segments: Global P&C Programs, Global Reinsurance, Global Accident & Health, and London Market Specialty. The Global P&C Programs segment offers programs space to clients and distribution partners. The Global Reinsurance segment provides casualty, property, and other specialties, such as proportional and excess of loss, treaty and facultative, aviation and space, marine and energy, and credit to insurance and reinsurance companies, government entities, and other risk bearing vehicles. The Global Accident & Health segment provides accident and health, property and casualty, aviation and space, credit, surety, marine and energy, and mortgage. The London Market Specialty segment provides London casualty, energy, property, and marine leaders services. The company offers medical insurance products, trip cancellation programs, medical management services, and 24/7 emergency medical and travel assistance services. The company was formerly known as Third Point Reinsurance Ltd. and changed its name to SiriusPoint Ltd. in February 2021. SiriusPoint Ltd. was incorporated in 2011 and is headquartered in Pembroke, Bermuda.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott  Egan ACMA, MBA | CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $3.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $35K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["SiriusPoint Ltd. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.1B market cap on $3.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +19% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 7.8\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 16.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 10% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2222222222222219},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 31% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How Siriuspoint Ltd. (SPNT) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/134/How_Siriuspoint_Ltd._SPNT_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111326044602_1794606362.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794606362.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SiriusPoint (SPNT), What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-spnt/siriuspoint/news/siriuspoint-spnt-what-is-behind-the-fresh-attention","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794533013.894,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Leuthold Group LLC Acquires 159,787 Shares of S